# Ada Bench

An open, reproducible retrospective benchmark for predicting clinical anti drug antibody (ADA) rates on FDA approved monoclonal antibodies - the de facto leaderboard ALP Bio can quote in every BD meeting.

## Why This Exists

The single most important question a pharma partner will ask Punit in a BD meeting is not "how does your organoid work?" - it is " how do I know your predictor generalises beyond what you trained on? " ADA risk is famously dataset fragile: most published immunogenicity predictors (e.g. NetMHCIIpan class predictors of MHC II binding) overfit to the small set of cleared biologics that have public clinical ADA data (NetMHCIIpan ref).

## What It Builds

- Replays synthetic `single` and `important` cases against the project's evidence rules.
- Scores `single_coverage`, `important_risk`, and `question_precision` so regressions are visible in CSV and JSON.
- Plants `single drift` and `important gap` failures as negative controls.
- Writes citation-locked decision claims; unsupported claims fail verification.
- Exports a review dashboard and demo pack for `ada-bench` without hosted services.

## Local Run

```bash
uv sync
uv run ada-bench all
uv run pytest -q
uv run ruff check .
```

## Outputs

- `outputs/analysis.json`
- `outputs/scenario_report.csv`
- `outputs/decision_report.md`
- `outputs/evidence_packet.md`
- `outputs/dashboard.html`
- `outputs/demo_pack.zip`

